mission "The Last Chartmaker's Errand"
    category "side"
    name "The Last Chartmaker's Errand"
    description "Carry a fragile chart folio from Bellweather Cay to San Aurelio, calling at Wreckers' Moon and Gallows Key to obtain two missing annotations."
    source "Bellweather Cay"
    waypoint "Wreckers' Moon" "Get Marda Quill's original soundings for the western passage."
    waypoint "Gallows Key" "Have Silas Rook authenticate the privateer mark on the chart."
    destination "San Aurelio"
    reward 1160
    to offer
        has "A Scholar Without a Flag"
    objective route
    speaker offer "Keeper Orlan"
    speaker waypoint_1 "Marda Quill"
    speaker waypoint_2 "Silas Rook"
    speaker visit "Brother Mateo"
    speaker complete "Keeper Orlan"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Keeper Orlan has spread a water-stained chart across the observatory table. Two sections have been cut away with a very sharp knife.`
            `"The missing marks are not decoration. One is a set of soundings kept by Marda Quill at Wreckers' Moon. The other is a privateer mark that Silas Rook at Gallows Key can identify. Take the folio to San Aurelio when both annotations are restored. Brother Mateo has agreed to keep it safe."`
            `The keeper ties the folio in oilcloth. "The calls matter. Wreckers' Moon first, Gallows Key second, San Aurelio last. A chart with only half its truth is worse than no chart at all."`
            choice
                `"I'll carry it and make each call in order."`
                    accept
                `"I have other business to attend to."`
                    close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Last Chartmaker's Errand. Follow Bellweather Cay → Wreckers' Moon → Gallows Key → San Aurelio, restoring the chart at each stop."
    on waypoint_1
        conversation
            `Marda Quill compares the folio with a battered notebook kept in a tarred leather case. She copies a set of soundings into the margin and marks a safe approach through the shoals.`
            `"There. I would not take a heavy ship through that water, but a careful captain will find room. Silas at Gallows Key will know the mark you are missing."`
    on waypoint_2
        conversation
            `Silas Rook turns the chart towards the light and gives a low whistle. He adds a small black pennant beside the soundings.`
            `"That mark belonged to the old Grey Gull privateers. It means the passage was watched, not owned. Take it to San Aurelio. Mateo will know why the old monastery kept a copy."`
    on visit
        conversation
            `Brother Mateo receives the folio with both hands. He checks Marda's soundings, then the privateer mark, and finally nods.`
            `"The annotations agree. This is the missing approach to the western archive. You have brought the pieces together without losing a single one."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Keeper Orlan's purse is heavier than you expected. "A chart is a promise made between one navigator and the next. You have helped keep this one honest."`
            `He gives you a copied note describing a quiet anchorage where pilots can shelter when the trade winds turn violent.`
        log "The chart folio was restored and delivered to San Aurelio. Keeper Orlan rewarded the voyage and shared a safe anchorage note."
